course: dictionary
lesson: 9281
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Spanish is a word with more than one meaning. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants. «Spanish scientists reported that eastern tree frogs in the zone are darker than usual.» Here Spanish means from Spain, because it tells you where the scientists come from.
explain: Spanish can also name a language. «speak Spanish» and «Spanish class» are about the language people talk and learn, not about a country or a person. Ask yourself: is this word describing something, or is it the name of a thing? That question helps you choose the right meaning.
explain: Spanish can name people too. «The Spanish forced Indigenous people to mine the silver mountain of Potosí in Bolivia.» Here The Spanish means the people of Spain. When Spanish has «the» in front of it and is about what people did, it is usually the people.
fact: Spanish can be an adjective, a noun for the language, or a noun for the people.
fact: Spanish is the language spoken in Spain and in most countries of Central and South America, like Mexico and Argentina.
fact: «The eastern bulge of Brazil» is a main reason Brazil speaks Portuguese, while most of South America speaks Spanish.
fact: English, Hindi, Russian, Spanish and Persian all belong to the Indo-European family of languages.
fact: Many pupils learn Spanish as a foreign language, especially in the USA, where many people speak it at home.
exercise: «Spanish scientists reported that eastern tree frogs in the zone are darker than usual.» Where do the scientists come from? | From Brazil | *From Spain | From Japan
exercise: Where is Spanish spoken? | Only in the USA | Only in Brazil | *In Spain and in most countries of Central and South America
exercise: «The Spanish forced Indigenous people to mine the silver mountain.» What does The Spanish mean here? | The frogs of the zone | Brazilian people | *The people of Spain | The silver miners
test: In «a Spanish guitar», what does Spanish tell you about the guitar? | It is the name of the guitar | It is the people who play it | *Where it comes from or what style it is | It is a language the guitar speaks
test: «Brazil speaks Portuguese while most of South America speaks what?» | English | Mandarin | *Spanish | Portuguese
exam: In «a Spanish omelette», what kind of word is Spanish? | *Adjective, a word that describes the omelette | Verb, an action word | Noun, the name of a language | Pronoun, a word that replaces a noun
